{
  "type": "initialChallenge",
  "content": {
    "tiles": [
      {
        "id": "xj18rBnYqYke3vQg",
        "title": "Text 5",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<h2><strong>CLUE&#x27;s Tools</strong></h2><p>In this section you will try out each of CLUE&#x27;s tools. Note: the tools in CLUE are updated often.</p><p>To use a tool, click on it and then move it to your workspace. To position it precisely, drag it from the toolbar to your workspace, move it to where you want, and let go. </p><p>To complete the Initial Challenge, you will practice basic functions with each of the following in your own workspace:</p><ol><li> Text</li><li> Table </li><li> Coordinate Grid</li><li> Graph</li><li>Coordinate Grid vs. Graph </li><li>Bar Graph</li><li> Sketch </li><li> Equation </li><li> Number Line</li><li> Image</li></ol><p><span data-slate-type=\"highlight\" data-slate-highlight-id=\"6fad4869-7543-40ce-8091-f7fc451d2d9b\"></span></p>"
          ],
          "highlightedText": [
            {
              "id": "6fad4869-7543-40ce-8091-f7fc451d2d9b",
              "text": "Follow the directions below to explore the tools and complete the Initial Challenge."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "5EnLE3kVRXGkSUKo",
        "title": "CLUE's Tools",
        "content": {
          "type": "Image",
          "url": "cmpclue/images/tool.jpg",
          "filename": "cmpclue/images/tool.jpg"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "lXYMiD4dmtl8Wuks",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p><u><strong>1. Text</strong></u></p><p>The text tool is like many other editors, but some options may work slightly differently.</p><ol><li>To select text, click in the text tile, then drag over the text or use the arrow keys with the Shift key to select by character or Command-Shift for larger selections. (On a PC, use the Ctrl key instead of the Command key.) Note: Dragging where there is no text moves the whole text tile.</li><li>To use an editing tool, select the text you want to format (e.g., bold, italicize, etc.), then click the tool, which will turn blue. Or click the tool first and start typing formatted text. </li><li>Be sure to click the tool again to deselect it when you’re done. </li></ol><p>When text is selected, you can use the usual keyboard shortcuts:</p><ul><li>Cut: Command-X</li><li>Copy: Command-C</li><li>Paste: Command-V</li><li>Undo: Command-Z</li><li>Redo: Command-Shift-Z</li><li>Select all text in a tile: Command-A</li></ul>"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "whAoduFA4bwVSOsg",
        "title": "Text Controls",
        "content": {
          "type": "Image",
          "url": "cmpclue/images/txt.jpg",
          "filename": "cmpclue/images/txt.jpg"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "0HAUh5MvxsocLXtD",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p><em>Drag this tile into the Initial Challenge section in your workspace, and format the text below as described.</em></p><p></p><p>Bold</p><p>Italic</p><p>Underline</p><p>Highlight <span data-slate-type=\"highlight\" data-slate-highlight-id=\"83baee5f-4444-4b58-9eef-f27cb9d416ea\"></span></p><p>Subscript</p><p>Superscript</p><p></p><p>Make this a</p><p>Numbered</p><p>List</p><p></p><p>Make this a</p><p>Bulleted</p><p>List</p>"
          ],
          "highlightedText": [
            {
              "id": "83baee5f-4444-4b58-9eef-f27cb9d416ea",
              "text": "(Note: Once you highlight something, you can no longer edit it)"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "QN5Ky2SAOa4Zp12i",
        "title": "Text 6",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p><u><strong>2. Table</strong></u></p><p>Use a table to relate two or more quantities. Tables can hold numbers or text. You can edit the table title or column labels by double-clicking. You can move from cell to cell with the tab key. </p><p><em>Drag the table below into the Initial Challenge section in your workspace.</em></p><p>Explore the table functions. </p><ul><li>Add another column and label it Height (ft.)</li><li>Fill the column with heights. You can make up the numbers (or research them, if you want)</li><li>Add another dinosaur or two and fill out the columns with made up (or researched) numbers</li></ul>"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "tv3HDnP_Uly6Q718",
        "content": {
          "type": "Table",
          "columnWidths": {
            "pi3rYVT7TKGBv2et": 110,
            "VS-JmSW1aJFmeQ8H": 146
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "wTbM3-AZp3Hj-T5o",
        "title": "Text 7",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p><u><strong>3. Coordinate Grid</strong></u></p><li>Coordinate grid is used for shapes and geometry because the grid is always square like graph paper. You can&#x27;t stretch or shrink the scales on the axes. </li><li></li><p><em>Drag the Coordinate Grid below into the Initial Challenge in your workspace.</em> Play with the shapes by doing the following:</p><ol><li>Change both the shapes to be the same color.</li><li>Duplicate the shapes and make a pattern of tiles by moving them and rotating them to face different ways.</li><li>Make a shape with 5 or more sides.</li><li>Make a circle.</li><li>Label a point, a line, and a shape with one of the available options.</li><li>Give the graph a background by using Upload Image</li></ol><p>Helpful hints: </p><ul><li>Use the arrow keys to nudge any selected object (points, lines, shapes) by 0.01 unit to get it exactly where you want it. </li><li>Control your view of the shapes with the Zoom In/Out and Fit all options as well as the navigator arrows on the bottom right of the tile. </li></ul>"
          ]
        }
      },
