      {
        "id": "FI922XLPs0BfIuZ2",
        "title": "Text 13",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p><u><strong>10. Image</strong></u></p><p>Use the image tool to add a picture or snapshot to your work. For example, you might want to do some of your work with a pencil and paper. You can take a picture of it with the computer’s camera and upload it to your workspace. Then, all your work is together and your teacher can easily see it.</p><p>You can upload an image three ways: (1) Drag an image (JPG, PNG) from your computer directly into your workspace, (2) Drag and drop an image into a new image tool, or (3) Use the Upload Image option below the image tool to upload the file.</p><p>Of course, you can always drag an image from a problem into your workspace.</p><p><em>Add a math related image to your workspace under the Initial Challenge heading.</em></p>"
          ]
        }
      },
